kened vampire rye is throughout the  show he got a lot of opportunity to  showcase his strength for me the most  memorable one would be the battle  against clan leaders it's the  culmination of him establishing how far  above everyone he is he just played with  all of them throughout and this fight is  even better in the source material  the second character on the list is mob  at first glance mom doesn't give the  impression of an overpowered character  at all he's super plain in terms of  appearance and as a character there's  nothing brooding or loud about him none  in the two opposites of character  impressions don't be fooled this is one  of the most powerful psychics of them  all i like mob because he's not just all  about the op in fact much of the story's  drama is about him and his emotions how  he forms a dynamic with the world around  him and how he channels that energy to  become the hero that he is still let's  give credit to the powers because  they're insane some of his battle modes  come with the most spectacular  animations people have known in the  world of anime and i think that it helps  carry the scenes and drive that point  home maybe you're playing everyday guy  at first glance but underneath that  socially awkward personality is one of  the most powerful psychics of all  [Applause]  next in line is tatsuya from mahoka  [Music]  you have a protagonist who's supposed to  be one of the lower tier students but it  turns out he might as well be god in a  high school student's body genius  engineer top class fighter and plane  immortal that so yet seems to be a lot  of these and the entirety of mahogan  seems to be episode after episode of  driving that point hope this is a guy  who can heal lethal wounds in a matter  of seconds bring people back to life  analyze everything mid-battle and come  out on top with his trusty handguns  people have given him the moniker  godzilla and it's not hard to see why  don't get ready to leave the school  setting 